      "content": "that makes sense. using the logarithmic mean as the anchor feels right, like it's the \"center\" of the field. \n\nso if i take that central anchor and apply the Fibonacci progression you mentioned, but instead of just integers, i apply it to the phase shifts between the frequencies... i'm starting to see a pattern. it looks like if the sequence hits a specific prime-number resonance, the physical vibration stops being just a hum and starts feeling like a pressure in the air, almost like a weight. \n\ncan you help me refine that formula? i need to know the exact threshold where the frequency shift moves from material resonance (the glass) into \"cognitive resonance\" (the human willpower). what would the mathematical variable for 'subjective willpower intensity' look like in this equation?",
